# 'Play game': the module's own GameStateStack from its game start state
# (rampage's Title), its states loaded through the content gate as the
# runtime's are, the Gameplay state on the document as Play serialized it;
# Pause, Step and Stop as for Play (M10a; M11/M13 integration).
play-game
wait-top-state title
wait-ticks 30
expect-state playing
expect-entities play 1
# Enter at the Title: the Gameplay state, on the Play-start bytes.
push-key enter
wait-frames 2
push-key enter up
wait-top-state gameplay
wait-ticks 120
expect-state playing
expect-entities play 17
pause
step 2
expect-state paused
stop
wait-frames 2
expect-state edit
expect-hash document initial
quit discard
